# Cell from playpick: mode=battleground map=flags spec=druid:feral
# style=auto view=1280x800 save=carried.
#
# First druid:feral this job has played, and the first mode=battleground
# session on a non-touch (desktop/mouse) viewport. `src/main.ts`'s hitAt()
# only answers `auto` when `input.isTouchMode()` is true (checked by reading
# the code before writing this), and README says the AUTO toggle is "touch
# only" -- so on 1280x800 there is no control for `style=auto` to tap, and
# playbot's own play() (scripts/playbot.ts:833-839) is written to notice that
# and fall back to playing `good` instead rather than waste the pull. That
# fallback has never been confirmed against an actual journal line before
# (the one prior style=auto/desktop session, 2026-09-24's mode=walk toward
# whisper, never checked for it) -- watching for `no-autocast-toggle` in the
# journal is the point of this script as much as the match itself. If it
# fires, this also incidentally becomes the good-style Ebb and Flow data
# point direction.md's #7 asks for ("a good-style run on either map, to see
# whether active play actually turns one of these around").
open
targets
shot front
tap battleground
shot bg-menu
targets
tap map:flags
shot flags-picked
targets
tap class:druid:feral
shot feral-picked
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot bg-start
state
ui
play auto 60
shot mid1
state
bill
wait 5
play auto 60
shot mid2
state
bill
wait 5
play auto 60
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
